drums.onnx — Pulse's drum model

A small transformer trained by Pulse (training code in ml/drums) on drum
parts taken from two datasets, both under the Creative Commons Attribution
4.0 International license (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/):

The Lakh MIDI Dataset v0.1
  Colin Raffel. "Learning-Based Methods for Comparing Sequences, with
  Applications to Audio-to-MIDI Alignment and Matching". PhD Thesis, 2016.
  https://colinraffel.com/projects/lmd/

The Groove MIDI Dataset v1.0.0
  Jon Gillick, Adam Roberts, Jesse Engel, Douglas Eck, and David Bamman.
  "Learning to Groove with Inverse Sequence Transformations." International
  Conference on Machine Learning (ICML), 2019.
  https://magenta.tensorflow.org/datasets/groove

From each part only its drum hits were kept, on a sixteenth-note grid, in
eight sounds and four strengths; the model learned from those.
